<title>FRANCE: French parliament backs rise in petrol duties.</title>
<headline>French parliament backs rise in petrol duties.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's National Assembly on Friday backed government proposals to raise petrol duties next year, by rejecting an amendment to prevent the increase.</p>
<p>The UDF party, junior partner in the ruling centre-right coalition, had supported an amendment to block government plans in the 1997 budget to raise petrol duties in line with inflation.</p>
<p>The lower house of parliament rejected the amendment by 100 votes to 63.</p>
</text>
